(HIVE - Demo Rulebook \(Board Game Cafe\)) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(OVERVIEW) Tj T*
(An abstract strategy game for 2 players with no board. The pieces form the hive.) Tj T*
(Surround your opponent's Queen Bee on all six sides to win.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(PIECES) Tj T*
(Each player has 11 pieces: 1 Queen Bee, 2 Spiders, 2 Beetles, 3 Grasshoppers and 3) Tj T*
(Soldier Ants.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(PLACING A PIECE) Tj T*
(On your turn either place a new piece or move a placed piece. A new piece must touch) Tj T*
(at least one of your own pieces and none of your opponent's \(the second piece of the) Tj T*
(game is the exception\). Your Queen Bee must be placed by your fourth turn. You can not) Tj T*
(move pieces until your Queen is placed.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(ONE HIVE RULE) Tj T*
(The pieces must stay connected at all times, also during a move. A piece whose removal) Tj T*
(would split the hive can not move.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(FREEDOM TO MOVE) Tj T*
(Pieces slide around the hive. A piece can not squeeze through a gap too narrow for it,) Tj T*
(except the Grasshopper and a Beetle climbing.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
